---
import SiteShell from "../components/SiteShell.astro";
---

<SiteShell title="Today" description="Today's work for the !localhost design sprint.">
    <div class="max-w-3xl py-14">
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest">Current class brief</p>
        <h1 class="mt-3 font-heading text-5xl">Today: make a first visit possible.</h1>
        <ol class="mt-12 space-y-7">
            <li class="grid gap-3 border-t border-gray-300 pt-6 sm:grid-cols-[3rem_1fr]">
                <span class="font-heading text-3xl" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
                <div><h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Choose one thing to put online</h2><p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed">Pick the smallest part of your project that someone can experience. A single interaction is enough. For a physical artefact, choose one behaviour, decision, or consequence to translate into a digital encounter.</p></div>
            </li>
            <li class="grid gap-3 border-t border-gray-300 pt-6 sm:grid-cols-[3rem_1fr]">
                <span class="font-heading text-3xl" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
                <div><h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Write the invitation</h2><p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed">In two sentences, tell a new visitor where they are and what they can do. Put this near the start of the experience. You can keep the mystery; give them a way in.</p></div>
            </li>
            <li class="grid gap-3 border-t border-gray-300 pt-6 sm:grid-cols-[3rem_1fr]">
                <span class="font-heading text-3xl" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
                <div><h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Draw one path</h2><p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed">On paper or in Figma: arrival → first action → what changes → what happens next. Mark any point where the visitor needs a clue, a response, or a way back. Use the sketch to guide your code, rather than drawing every screen first.</p></div>
            </li>
            <li class="grid gap-3 border-t border-gray-300 pt-6 sm:grid-cols-[3rem_1fr]">
                <span class="font-heading text-3xl" aria-hidden="true">04</span>
                <div><h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Build and share a rough version</h2><p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed">Get that path working in a browser and put it on a public URL. Open the link on your phone. If it fails, write down what failed and make the smallest fix that lets someone continue.</p></div>
            </li>
        </ol>

        <aside class="mt-12 border-l-4 border-[#a9d400] bg-white p-5 shadow-sm">
            <h2 class="font-semibold">Before you leave</h2>
            <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed">Have a link and a one-path sketch. If the link isn’t live yet, bring the exact thing that stopped you so we can solve it together.</p>
        </aside>
        <p class="mt-8 text-sm">Stuck on structure, interaction, or screen sizes? Try <a class="text-link" href="/resources/from-local-to-live">From local to live</a>.</p>
    </div>
</SiteShell>
